WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.320
Exam hall.

2
00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.150
The clock is running.

3
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.280
On the desk, a passage
you have never seen.

4
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:10.250
Student one picks up the pen and
starts writing straight away.

5
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.260
Rewind.

6
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.470
Student two reads the page
three times, jots a few notes,

7
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.380
and only then begins.

8
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.580
Same passage.

9
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:19.830
Same time.

10
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.220
So why not start writing at once?

11
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:25.820
In this mission, you'll see what
Paper 1 puts in front of you:

12
00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.280
unseen passages, each
with a guiding question.

13
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:33.610
You'll ask what a first read can
miss, and what a second one is for.

14
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.700
And you'll decide whether a plan
is worth the minutes it costs.

15
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: explain why you
shouldn't start writing at once.
